title: Questline
---
<<wait 2>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>


<<if $bigJob == false>>
    <<jump DivorcedDad>>
<<else>>
    <<jump Influencer>>
<<endif>>
===


title: DivorcedDad
---
///////////////// Play Luxury Apt 02 music track
///////////////// Show lobby environment art
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
The delivery takes me to the Meridian District, home to the tech zillionaires and their corporate grifters. I approach a high-end luxury apartment tower and feel its tinted windows judge me as I park my motorbike right outside the entrance. 
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
Nubs: W-Wait up!
The glass lobby doors swing open, and I step inside to search for the owner of this sad bag of food.
A man in an outdated puffer vest and overpriced pants immediately walks over, waving at me.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Dad>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadNeutral>>
???: Delivery for Benji?
Luna: Yeah.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
Benji: Hey, you're from Root Town, right?
He points at my motorbike's decal—a large gnarled tree, and the symbol of Root Town. 
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
Luna: (The guy's got some crazy vision with those glasses…) 
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutralArms>>
Benji: I'm from Root Town, too. HELLA!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: (And he's hella cringe.)
I shove the order into the man's hands and mark my order as complete on the SL0P app without another word.
But he lingers in the lobby. 
Luna: (It feels like he's REALLY desperate to say something, but has no one to say it to.)


-> Ignore him and leave
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadAnnoyed>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    I turn around and leave. A job's a job, and I finished it.
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    //I imagine a black screen and the dialogue box
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app and a violation as the cherry on top. It said the food looked like it'd been tampered with…
    Luna: …
    Nubs: I was hungry…
    But who cares? A person who lives in that building is rich enough to get more food without batting an eye…
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>
-> Stare at him, expecting him to talk
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
    Benji: Giving me the Gen Z stare, huh?
    Luna: No one says that. That's like 40 years old.
    Luna: (Which is probably how old he is. Or even older.)
    Luna: What do you want?
    Benji: Oh, you've got time? Awesome! I'm glad the SL0P app still hires humans and gives their employees—er, contractors—paid breaks.
    Luna: We don't. And time's ticking.


Benji: I just HAVE to tell someone. I'm going to get my first AGENTS implant tomorrow! I'm going all-in on eye surgery. Not even the best AGENTS glasses can beat an implant's eyesight. 
Luna: (So that's why his vision was so creepy good…)
Benji: My doc said I should be on an all-liquid diet for best results. But tomorrow, I'll be a new man who can finally stop eating sad soups!
He opens his delivery bag and frowns.
<<set $badend += 1>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadAnnoyed>>
Benji: Hey, what gives!? Where's my side order of ion kelp crystals!?
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
I look down at my feet, where Nubs is. Glowing green goop is smeared across his screen.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
Nubs: Oops.
Luna: (How does he even eat?)
<<jump DivorcedDad_Surgery>>
===


title: DivorcedDad_Surgery
---
The man isn't happy—and I can't afford another violation on the SL0P app.
Luna: (He was yapping about his dumb surgery. Maybe I can distract him…)


-> Ask him about the AGENTS implant
    Luna: Why are you getting the surgery?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
    Benji: Yes, my surgery!
-> Congratulate him sarcastically
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
    Luna: Congrats. I'm sure your surgery will be SO life-changing…
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
    Benji: Thank you! I'm excited for it, too.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
    Nubs: …
    Luna: (Ugh. Not you, too…)
-> Leave him and go
    Luna: Time to bounce.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    Nubs: I'm not sure that was a good idea…
    // Motorcycle SFX sound
    <<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
    I scoop up the creature and put him back on my motorbike. I ride away, leaving the deadbeat customer in a cloud of smoke to choke on.
    Because fuck AGENTS.
        <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    //I imagine a black screen and the dialogue box
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app and a violation as the cherry on top. It said the food looked like it'd been tampered with.
    Thanks, Nubs…
    But who cares? A person who lives in that building is rich enough to get more food without batting an eye…
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>
Benji: I'm getting it because all the guys I work with already have something augmented.
Benji: They got their hands done to type faster, or their brains to sync directly with the company's internal systems. Plus, I'll finally be able to ditch the glasses and look less chopped.
Luna: (Who's gonna tell him…)
Benji: This is a dream job. Everyone in Root Town wants to be me.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadNeutral>>
Benji: But I need to keep up. I can't fall behind.
<<jump DivorcedDad_Questions>>
===






title: DivorcedDad_Questions
---
-> Why do you feel behind? <<once>>
    Benji: Because I'm not getting the same amount of sales leads as my peers. And I KNOW it's because I'm not optimized with the same implants as they are. Clients also take you more seriously when you're augmented.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Benji: More implants means more clients, which means more money.
    Luna: And that eventually leads to…?
    Benji: Financial freedom! And the time to finally do whatever I want. Heck, I might even become the CEO of my own company!
    Benji: AGENTS take 75% of what I make, though…
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
    Benji: But that's late-stage capitalism, baby!
    Luna: (He doesn't need surgery. He's already delusional.)
    //Return to the set of the questions in this mode, but remove this question or block it out since the player has already received the answer for this question.
    <<jump DivorcedDad_Questions>>
-> Where did you work in Root Town?
    Benji: You know the story. A low-paying sales job with grueling work hours.
    Benji: But once I got this job at AGENTS, everything changed. I got relocated to this swanky tower, free food, and a personal droid that chauffeurs me to and from the office.
    Benji: It was all just for me, though. The contract didn't include my family. Just 80 hour days, seven days a week. I thought it'd pay off.
    Benji: Not quick enough, though. Divorce papers were mailed to my apartment within months of starting at AGENTS.
        -> You would put work before family? Yikes…
            <<set $badend += 1>>
            <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadAnnoyed>>
            Benji: You're one to talk. You don't have a wife and kid.
            Luna: Pretty rude to assume, unc.
            Benji: It felt like it was worth the cost. But now…
        -> That sounds kinda unfair to them, tbh.
            <<set $goodend += 1>>
            Benji: Well IMO, it felt like it was worth the cost.
            Benji: It's easy to take the side you haven't heard.
            Benji: But now…
        -> And did it feel like the right choice?
            Benji: At the time, yes. 
            Benji: But now…
-> Where do you work now? <<once>>
    Benji: I work for AGENTS. It'd be weird if I didn't stand by the product I work for, right? It's like a rite of passage.
    //Return to the set of the questions in this mode, but remove this question or block it out since the player has already received the answer for this question.
    <<jump DivorcedDad_Questions>>


I hear his voice crack, then taper off into the dead air between us.
<<jump HelpBenji>>
===




title: HelpBenji
---
<<declare $timetime = 0>>
Benji: Everything I'm doing now…it was to spend more time with them.
Benji: You wouldn't understand…


-> If that's what you wanna believe.
    Luna: Everyone makes choices. You just made yours.
    Benji: Yeah…
    He seems satisfied with my answer, but I still hear doubt in his voice.
    Luna: (Look at me, talking about choices with an ultra-rich sellout. Like I'm one to talk…)
-> Hope your kid is proud of you for selling your soul.
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadAnnoyed>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    Benji: Fuck off! I hope you rot like the rest of Root Town.
    Nubs: I'm not sure that was a good idea…
    Luna: Whatever. The last thing Root Town needs is a traitor and a sellout.
    // Motorcycle SFX sound
    <<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
    <<exit SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
    I rev my bike's engine and ride off with Nubs.
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    //I imagine a black screen and the dialogue box
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app and a violation as the cherry on top. It said the food looked like it'd been tampered with.
    Thanks, Nubs…
    But who cares? A person who lives in that building and sells his soul to AGENTS is clearly rich enough to get more food…
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>
-> You're never gonna get back that time, though.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<set $timetime = 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
    Luna: You've probably missed out on school performances, birthdays, maybe even a graduation. And all the small wins in between.
    Benji: …
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: But that doesn't mean you can't take back time now. That's a choice.
    Nubs: Luna…
    Benji: And life is full of choices…
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
    Benji: Damn, you're one wise delivery driver! Have you ever considered becoming a life coach?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
    Luna: I'd probably make millions if it was this easy.
    Luna: (But it's true. This gig job is a choice…and it might not be too late to change it up.)
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadNeutral>>
    Benji: I'm gonna call my ex-wife tonight. Hear my daughter's voice. It's time to start making up for all that lost time.


Benji: Thanks for listening to an old, uncool guy.
Nubs: …
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadHappy>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
Benji: Oh! Is that a talking cyberpet?
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWave>>
Nubs: I am not a pet! I am a super secret weap—!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappyShy>>
Luna: Y-Yeah, he's a pet! Did you know they're gonna let pets speak 25 different languages soon?
Nubs: Hey! That's proprietary information!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Dad dadNeutral>>
Benji: Where have I heard that before? Was it in an internal post at AGENTS…?
Luna: G-Gotta go!
// Motorcycle SFX sound
<<sfx SceneSampleEvents tires>>
I scoop up Nubs, dump him onto my motorbike, and ride off into the night.
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<exit SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
//I imagine a black screen and the dialogue box
20 minutes later, I get an extra tip notification and a five-star rating from Benji.
Maybe there's more to Frisscity folk than meets the eye…
<<jump DivorcedDad_Good_Outcome>>
===




title: DivorcedDad_Good_Outcome
---
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
///////////////// Play Sunday Neons music track
//////////// Show The Bridge environment art
I wrap up my delivery job with Nubs and make my way over to The Bridge.
The shadow of Root Town lingers in the distance across the ocean.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
///////////// Show new phone message opportunities by showing the new notification status on the cyberdeck’s NATIO 3000 logo
// If player chose You’re never gonna get back that time, then also show the below:
<<if $timetime == 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShy>>
    Luna: (A life coach, huh? Kaya would laugh. She's better at that touchy-feely stuff.)
    Nubs: So this is the Gen Z stare…
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Stop saying that. It's like, SO old.
    Luna: He's probably from that generation.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
    Nubs: Yeah. Like, HELLA old.
    Luna: Ugh, stop being cringe. Remove that from your memory. Or hardware, or…whatever it's called!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsLoading>>
    Beeping noises echo from Nubs's miniature metal body.
    Nubs: Got it. I'll archive “hella” “cringe,” and “Gen Z stare” into my database and categorize them by history and by social settings.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    Luna: We need to program something in you that actually LISTENS to me…
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
<<endif>>
// Continue with the below text. If player didn’t choose You’re never gonna get back that time, then just show the below:
I notice Nubs is lost in thought.
Luna: What's wrong?
Nubs: I am thinking about what Benji said. About the time he lost because of his job at AGENTS. My emotions radar picked up feelings of sadness and loneliness.
Nubs: I can only infer that this sadness is caused by AGENTS.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
Luna: AGENTS is bad.
Nubs: But why is AGENTS bad? Our mission is to help humankind advance towards a new evolutional frontier. Benji was in the process of doing that.
Luna: But he was doing it for himself—and ONLY himself. Your company's little “mission statement” is a complete lie. AGENTS doesn't help, it only harms.
Luna: You heard it from Benji. AGENTS gave him money and clout, but it shattered his family life into bits.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
Luna: He couldn't have both, so he chose to sell his soul to AGENTS. That's what AGENTS does. It takes away your humanity.
Nubs: I see…
Luna: And if we wanna keep talking about selling souls, then just look over there.
I point over to Root Town and the smoke that billows from buildings in the distance.
Luna: That's what AGENTS did to my hometown. To me.
Luna: They rely on us to power their services. And in return? They force us to work low-paying jobs on the apps they built.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: I'm an example of that.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
Nubs: …
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
I'm clearly bumming the little guy out.
Luna: Obviously you can tell I hate it. But…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
Luna: Meeting Benji got me thinking. Maybe I've been judging everyone who lives here a little too quickly.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
Luna: He said life is full of choices…and choosing to waste my life away on this trashy SL0P app is a choice.
Luna: I just have to…own it.
Nubs: Luna…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyWave>>
Nubs: You're hella cool right now!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShy>>
Luna: S-Shut up! I still hate AGENTS. And what your master does.
Nubs giggles. It sounds like a series of high-pitched chirps.
It's actually pretty cute.
<<jump LilGuy_Respite>>
// You can find this node in the Climax.yarn tab
===




title: Influencer
---
///////////////// Play Luxury Apt 02 music track
///////////////// Show apartment hallway environment art
<<wait 2>>
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
The delivery takes me to the Meridian District, home to the tech zillionaires and their corporate grifters.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
I haul a catering order through the bulletproof glass doors of a luxury apartment and trudge past the security robots in the lobby. They don't press the elevator button for me.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
Because they know I don't belong here.
I'm taken to the top floor and eventually find the apartment number that matches the one on my screen. I press a button on their intercom's sleek glass pad. 
Then I wait.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
…And wait.


-> Continue to wait
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngry>>
    Luna: Sigh…
    Nubs: How long do you intend to dally at the door? 
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedWave>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Nubs: Ah!
    His tail thwacks one of the bags and it falls over. Green slush oozes out from the bag and stains a very expensive-looking doormat.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
    Luna: Shit.
    I try to blot the mess away with a wad of napkins I found hidden in one of the other bags. Now it looks worse, like a muddy mess.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    Nubs: Oops.
    Luna: …      
-> Press the button again
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    Luna: I don't have all day, divas.
    Nubs: Ah. So the owners of this abode are female versions of a hustler?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedShy>>
    Luna: W-What?! No. Where are you even-? Ugh. Nevermind.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngry>>
    I press the button again on the glass interface. Time's ticking, and I can feel the little creature's beady little eyes on my back. I know what I promised him.
    Nubs: How long do you intend to dally at the door?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedWave>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Nubs: Ah!
    His tail thwacks one of the bags and it falls over. Green slush oozes out from the bag and stains a very expensive-looking doormat.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
    Luna: Shit.
    I try to blot the mess away with a wad of napkins I found hidden in one of the other bags. Now it looks worse, like a muddy mess.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    Nubs: Oops.
    Luna: …      
-> Take a photo of the order and leave
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    Luna: I don't have time for this.
    I snap a photo on the SL0P app to prove that I left the order at the correct location. I make sure to capture the apartment's number.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedWave>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Nubs: Ah!
    The creature's tail thwacks one of the bags and it falls over. Green slush oozes out from the bag and stains a very expensive-looking doormat.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
    Luna: Shit.
    I try to blot the mess away with a wad of napkins I found hidden in one of the other bags. Now it looks worse, like a muddy mess.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedWave>>
    Nubs stands and watches as I try to clean up his mess. He obviously wants to say something, but I don't let him.
    Luna: Let's just get out of here.
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app AND a violation as the cherry on top. It notes the doormat stain as damaged property.
    But who cares? A person who lives in this building is rich enough to buy anything without blinking an augmented eye…
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>
<<jump Influencer_Continued>>
===




title: Influencer_Continued
---
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
The door clicks open.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Influencer>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerNeutral>>
A woman with impeccable hair stands in the doorway. I notice a bead wedged in between her eyes and realize it’s an AGENTS implant.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
???: Heyo, fam! My catering order from SL0P just arrived. Powered by AGENTS, of course! I always try to shop local and support real human labor in our economy~!


Her followers get to see the bags—and the stain on her doormat—before she does.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>>
<<set $badend += 1>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
???: (I feel like I've seen her before. But where…)


-> Ask if she's been in an ad before
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
    ???: Are you talking about my downtown billboard in the beauty district? Or maybe my limited-edition cosmetic line in collaboration with Mr. Bae-zos 2.0?
    She moves her cyberphone so that I'm viewable to her live audience, which makes me freeze in place.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    ???: Look, everyone! My delivery gal is a Queenie fan! Part of the royal fam.
    Luna: (“Fan?” Hell no. I didn't ask to be on someone's livestream…)
-> Ask for her name, using the delivery as an excuse
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
    ???: It's Queenie! Ohmigods, you've never heard of me before!?
    She moves her cyberphone so that I'm viewable to her audience, which makes me freeze in place.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
    Queenie: Can you believe this, my royal fam? My delivery girl doesn't know who I am!
    Luna: (I'm not getting paid to be on someone's livestream…)
-> Just take a photo and leave
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>> 
    ???: Hey! You need to pay for that!
    Luna: It's a photo of the food. If I don't take one, I get fired.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Or do you not support “human labor”?
    ???: Rrrgh!
    I hear notifications and reaction noises ping from the woman's phone. Before I can give her followers more tea, I turn around and make my way back down to the lobby.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
    Nubs: I'm not sure that was a good idea…
    Luna: Let's just get out of here.
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app AND a violation as the cherry on top. It notes the doormat stain as damaged property.
    But who cares? A person who lives in that building is rich enough to buy anything without blinking an augmented eye…
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>


<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsLoading>>
Nubs: Queenie. Beauty influencer. 800 million followers. Blood type O. Leo rising. Use discount code ROYALGUARD for 33% off your first AGENTS implant! Terms apply.
And then, it hits me.
Luna: (Wait, THIS is the influencer Kaya raves about?)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
Queenie: Ohmigods, fam! Look at this cute cyberpet!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngry>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>> 
Luna: (Shit! I can't have her livestream a damn war machine to millions of people!)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedShy>> 
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsConfused>>
Luna: N-No cameras! He's…he's got a location tracker on him! So everyone will know where you live!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsLoading>>
Nubs: I do. I can begin broadcasting our coordinates right now…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>>
Queenie: What the-?! 
Luna: Turn it off!
Queenie: Okay, okay! Geez. 
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
Queenie: Signing off for a bit fam! Be back soon~
She blows a kiss to her followers and ends the stream.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerNeutral>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
Queenie: That was close. I can't let my crazy fans know where I live.
Queenie: And I can't have another girl from Root Town rat me out.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>> 
Luna: Rat you out?
I try to remember why Kaya likes Queenie so much.
Queenie: Can you finish up and go? My followers need me…
<<jump Queenie_Questions>>
===




title: Queenie_Questions
---
-> Could I get a selfie? <<once>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
    The frown says it all. “No.”
    //Return back to the set of questions in this node, but remove this question since the player completed it.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerNeutral>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
    <<jump Queenie_Questions>>
-> Aren't you also from Root Town?
    Queenie: Yeah. So? Are you here to cancel me?
    -> Why would I cancel you?
        <<set $goodend += 1>>
        Luna: I don't even know you. Well, my friend does. But why would I cancel someone I barely know?
        Luna: (Even if she makes it pretty easy to hate her…)
        Queenie: True. I guess I'm just a little paranoid.
    -> (Jokingly) I'll write a post about how awful you were IRL
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>> 
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeturalArms>> 
        Queenie: You wouldn't.
        Luna: I've seen my fair share of bad reviews. Got some sick disses archived.
        Queenie: I can only imagine the crazy shit you get dinged for.
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
        Luna: (And she wouldn't? I just messed up her doormat.)
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerNeutral>>
    -> Give me some baecoins and I won't do it.
        <<set $badend += 1>>
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>> 
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>> 
        Queenie: Stop giving Root Town a bad rep like that.
        <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>


Queenie: I'm used to the hate I get from Root Town. They call me a sellout.
Queenie: Because I'm from there and got famous for reviewing beauty products. Then chameleoned my way into Frisscity. I started promoting AGENTS makeup more and more.
Queenie: The next step was to become a walking ad for AGENTS implants. They made it easy for me, too. But my life isn't as glamorous as it looks.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>>
Queenie: I'm forced to keep subscriptions so that my implant stays on the latest model, or else it'll corrode my skin. AGENTS also keeps 70% of my sales revenue.
Nubs: …
Queenie: Now all I do is force discount codes for implant surgeries down everyone's throats. Surgeries I KNOW they can't afford.
Queenie: I want to give back, to actually make a difference. Maybe I'm really just a sellout…
<<jump Queenie_Ideas>>
===




title: Queenie_Ideas
---
<<declare $sample = 0>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>


-> Instead of selling AGENTS, find another way to help the Town.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerNeutral>>
    Queenie: Like what?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Like…don't gatekeep what comes after, about the costs and subscriptions. Be real with them, like how you're being real with me.
    Luna: Or, use your money to give back to Root Town.
    Queenie: Like for schools?
    Luna: Yeah. Or for infrastructure. Or food banks. We'll take anything at this point. But school is a start.
    Queenie: Maybe like…beauty school?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
    Luna: Yeah! What's the one you went to?
    Queenie: The one down by Lake M.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappyShy>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
    Luna: Did you ever try Chester's Cheesecakes before he got shut down?
    Queenie: Girl, my school was right next to his shop.
    We both find ourselves laughing, sharing a piece of Root Town history that only locals could know.
    Queenie: God, I miss Root Town. This riffing sesh really helped me remember why I love it.
    Luna: Yeah, well. Dreaming is all we CAN do at this point.
    Queenie: Maybe, maybe not. You're the driver of your own life.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
    Luna: …
    Queenie: Don't worry, I won't get philosophical. You've given me enough to think about.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Pay me in royalties for the idea. Or an extra tip.
    Queenie: How about a beauty sample, too? A SIGNED beauty sample?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Honestly, just the tip is—
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprisedArms>>
    Luna: (Wait. I know someone who'd want something like that—and who could possibly knock some off my rent if I gave her this!)
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappyArms>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: Actually yeah, I'll take it. Could you address it to “Kaya?” That's K-A-Y-A.
    <<set $sample = 1>>
    ///////////////Show the item asset: beauty sample addressed to Kaya
    Queenie: Done.
    I take the beauty product from her porcelain hands and slip it into my back pocket.
    Queenie: So now I know Kaya. But who is my hella mysterious and wise midnight delivery girl?
    Luna: It's Luna.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
    Queenie: Okay, Luna. And her cute little sidekick that can track locations.
    Nubs: I can do a lot more for people who have AGENTS implants. Like-
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Luna: D-Don't mind him! I installed a new microchip that allows him to talk. It's still a little buggy.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs snubsAngryArms>>
    Nubs: I'm not buggy! I've been cleared of 31 SEVs and over 2,000 coding errors!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>>
    Luna: V-Vaccinations! Sooo many vaccinations. Pets are so expensive, y'know?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWave>>
    Nubs: I. AM NOT. A PET!!
    I laugh it off as I quickly shuffle me and my alien away from Queenie's door so she doesn't get any ideas. I also make sure to take a picture of the delivery so SL0P doesn't ride my ass.
-> Just keep doing you. You need to give people time.
    <<set $goodend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
    Luna: People will come around. You said so yourself, you're from Root Town. So stay rooted.
    Luna: Maybe you've changed people's lives. Have those people talk about how much you helped them. You can't fake that.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutralArms>>
    Nubs: Luna…
    Queenie: That's not a bad idea. Especially from someone who hates AGENTS.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerHappy>>
    Queenie: Thanks, my hella mysterious and wise midnight delivery girl! And her cute little sidekick who can track locations.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
    Nubs: I can do a lot more for people who have AGENTS implants. Like-
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprised>>
    Luna: D-Don't mind him! I installed a new microchip that allows him to talk. It's still a little buggy.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryArms>>
    Nubs: I'm not buggy! I've been cleared of 31 SEVs and over 2,000 coding errors!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappy>>
    Luna: V-Vaccinations! Sooo many vaccinations. Pets are so expensive, y'know?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWave>>
    Nubs: I. AM NOT. A PET!!
    I laugh it off as I quickly shuffle me and my alien sidekick away from Queenie's door so she doesn't get any ideas. I also make sure to take a picture of the delivery so SL0P doesn't ride my ass.
-> Internet trolls are a small price to pay for your flex city life.
    <<set $badend += 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Influencer influencerAnnoyed>>
    Queenie: Wow, you don't have to be a bitch about it! 
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>     
    Luna: You live in a penthouse suite where everything's delivered to your door. And you STILL can't take cancel culture? It's giving privileged sob story.
    Queenie: Get out of my face. We're done.
    She slams the door, leaving me and the rest of the food on her stained doormat.
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
    Nubs: I don't think that was a good idea…
    I ignore the creature and instead snap a photo of the delivery because I need to prove that I did it correctly. A job's a job.
    <<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
    <<wait 2>>
    20 minutes later, I get a negative rating on the SL0P app AND a violation as the cherry on top. It notes the doormat stain as damaged property.
    But who cares? A person who lives in that building is clearly rich enough to buy anything they want without blinking an augmented eye…
    <<jump Bad_Outcome>>


<<fadeOut SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
20 minutes later, I get an extra tip notification and a five-star rating from Queenie!
Maybe there's more to Frisscity than meets the eye…
<<jump Influencer_Good_Outcome>>
===


title: Influencer_Good_Outcome
---
///////////////// Play Sunday Neons music track
//////////// Show The Bridge environment art
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
I wrap up my delivery job with Nubs and make my way over to The Bridge.
The shadow of Root Town lingers in the distance across the ocean.
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
////////// Show new phone message opportunities by showing the new notification status on the cyberdeck’s NATIO 3000 logo
// If player received the beauty sample addressed to Kaya, then also show the below:
<<if $sample == 1>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaSurprisedArms>>
    Luna: (I hate to admit it, but riffing with Queenie was kinda cool.)
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaHappyArms>>
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyArms>>
    Luna: (And now, Kaya will owe me 1,000 favors.)
    Nubs: You're hella thinking about Queenie, aren't you?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>>
    Luna: Hell no. Also, when did you start saying “hella”?
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsLoading>>
    Nubs: I observed your conversation and picked up a few things. Before you rudely called me a pet and pushed me away before I could fully scan her personal information.
    Luna: You'll pick up more slang when we go to Root Town. The more you talk like a local, the better you’ll blend in.
    Nubs: This vernacular is much more fascinating and complex than overused acronyms…like T.A.B.
    Luna: So you admit it was a dumb name!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsAngryWave>>
    Nubs: No I don't! I would not admit to such a thing!
    <<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
<<endif>>
// Continue with the below text. If the player didn’t receive the beauty sample addressed to Kaya, then just show the below:
I notice Nubs is lost in thought.
Luna: What's wrong?
Nubs: I'm thinking about what Queenie said. My emotions radar picked up feelings of sadness and stress.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>> 
Nubs: I can only infer that this sadness came from AGENTS.
Luna: Well, yeah. AGENTS is bad.
Nubs: But why is AGENTS bad? Our mission is to help humankind advance towards a new evolutional frontier.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>> 
Luna: You heard Queenie. She's trapped in a never-ending cycle of subscriptions that AGENTS cornered her into after she got her skin implant.
Luna: She relies on AGENTS to live. And relying on something isn't a choice. It's parasitic.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>> 
Nubs: I see…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutral>> 
Luna: And if we wanna keep talking about parasites, then look over there.
I point over to Root Town and the smoke that billows from its buildings in the distance.
Luna: That's what AGENTS did to my home. To me.
Luna: Frisscity relies on Root Town for people who will do their dirty work. And Root Town relies on Frisscity for jobs, even if they're at criminal prices.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
Luna: I'm a prime example of that.
Nubs: …
Nubs: Perhaps I am a parasite…
Luna: (Damn, I'm clearly bumming the little guy out.)
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralShy>>
Luna: But meeting Queenie got me thinking. Maybe I've been judging everyone who lives here a little too harshly.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
Luna: Queenie actually wants to help Root Town. She wants to fight that “us versus them” kinda mentality. That's deep.
Luna: I've always blamed Frisscity for my shitty situation. And for my shitty job. But maybe it's not as black and white as that…
Nubs: Luna…
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsHappyWave>>
Nubs: Omigods, you're HELLA cool right now!
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaShy>>
Luna: S-Shut up, don't read too much into it! I still hate AGENTS and what your master does.
Nubs laughs for the first time and it sounds like a series of high-pitched chirps.
It's…honestly pretty cute.
<<jump LilGuy_Respite>>
// You can find this node in the Climax.yarn tab
===




title: Bad_Outcome
---
///////////////// Play Sunday Neons music track
///////////////// Show The Bridge environment art
<<fadeIn SceneSampleEvents>>
<<wait 2>>
I wrap up my delivery job and make my way over to The Bridge. The shadow of Root Town lingers in the distance across the ocean.
I'm one step closer to sending this creature back to where he came from.
////////////////// Show new phone message opportunities by showing the new notification status on the cyberdeck’s NATIO 3000 logo
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Luna>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaNeutralArms>>
<<enter SceneSampleEvents Nubs>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsNeutral>>
Nubs seems lost in thought.
Luna: What's wrong?
Nubs: I'm thinking about the delivery and the emotions my mood radar picked up during it all.
Nubs: I was getting readings of sadness. And anger.
Nubs: From you.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorried>>
Luna: That whole job was a hassle—and you made it worse.
Nubs: Then why do you do it? Why do you work for AGENTS, when you hate it so much?
I could feel my face getting redder, getting hotter.
Luna: Why do I do it?! Because I HAVE to. Look.
I point over to Root Town and the smoke that billows from its buildings in the distance.
Luna: I know you've lived in a lab for your whole short-lived life, so I'll get you up to speed.
Luna: Frisscity relies on Root Town for people who will do their dirty work. Root Town relies on Frisscity for jobs, even if they're at criminal prices.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyed>>
Luna: That's what AGENTS does to my home. To me.
Nubs: …
Luna: I don't have a degree, the backdoor connections, or the money to get in. Hell, I'm barely able to keep a room in a crappy warehouse.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Luna lunaAnnoyedArms>>
Luna: There's nothing I can do. These were the cards life gave me.
Nubs: …
Luna: Congrats on illegally scanning me, by the way. Again.
<<show SceneSampleEvents Nubs nubsWorriedArms>>
I was clearly bumming the little guy out. But I didn't care.
Nubs: Our mission is to help humankind advance towards a new evolutionary frontier, not to hinder it. I do not understand.
Nubs: Despite this…
<<jump LilGuy_Respite>>
// You can find this node in the Climax.yarn tab
===



